// --aie-check-deadlock on the designs the oracle is checked on.

// The measured head-of-line pair (npu2): 9 extra words hang whatever the
// fabric holds; 8 finish only because the path holds 8, which the pass does
// not count on; issued the other way round, both finish.
// RUN: not aie-opt --aie-check-deadlock %S/Inputs/hw_head_of_line_k9.mlir -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=K9
// K9: error: dispatching @first_a deadlocks
// K9-DAG: note: the host waits for a completion token from (0, 0) S2MM 0
// K9-DAG: note: core (0, 2) waits to acquire cb (holds 0, wants 1)
// K9-DAG: note: (0, 2) S2MM 0 waits to acquire pa (holds 0, wants 1)
// K9-NOT: @first_b
// RUN: not aie-opt --aie-check-deadlock %S/Inputs/hw_head_of_line_k8.mlir -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=K8
// K8: error: dispatching @first_a deadlocks unless the fabric buffers more than it is known to
// K8-NOT: @first_b
// RUN: aie-opt --aie-check-deadlock=allow-undecided %S/Inputs/hw_head_of_line_k8.mlir -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=K8W
// K8W: warning: dispatching @first_a deadlocks unless

// Outside the subset: two cores race for a lock, and a channel nothing
// programs.
// RUN: not aie-opt --aie-check-deadlock %S/Inputs/contended_lock.mlir -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RACE
// RACE: error: cannot decide whether dispatching @run can deadlock
// RACE: note: a lock more than one agent acquires (l): which gets it first is not proven
// RUN: not aie-opt --aie-check-deadlock %S/Inputs/hidden_channel.mlir -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HIDDEN
// HIDDEN: note: a stream into (0, 1) S2MM 0, which the design does not program

// A dispatch that ends with a transfer stuck halfway.
// RUN: not aie-opt --aie-check-deadlock %S/Inputs/unquiesced.mlir -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FLIGHT
// FLIGHT: error: dispatching @run ends with work still in flight
// FLIGHT: note: (0, 2) S2MM 0 has 4 words in front of it nobody took

// An objectFIFO design lowered by aie-opt: lock amounts computed from
// loop-carried values, accepted.
// RUN: sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu2/' %S/../npu-xrt/add_one_objFifo/aie.mlir | aie-opt --aie-place-tiles --aie-objectFifo-stateful-transform --aie-check-deadlock -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OBJFIFO --allow-empty
// OBJFIFO-NOT: {{error|warning}}
